BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Neighborhood Cocktail Hour and Ratepayer Town Hall — Sebastopol 
 Center For the Arts\, California
DTSTART:20260828T000000
DTEND:20260829T000000
UID:afdca426cc1c51c36a8a4fdaa13f9d5e@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Neighborhood Cocktail Hour and Ratepayer Town Hall\n\n  \n    
 \n      \n      from $10.00\n    \n  \n\nFriday\, August 28 -5:30-6 Recept
 ion/Cocktails 6-7:30 Artist TalkDescription - Conceptual artist Kate Hau
 g spent the last 3 years of her life (so you don't have to!)  investigati
 ng how the City of Sebastopol administers the local water and sewer system
 . Spurned on by the question that is on everyone's mind - "Why is my water
  bill so high?" - Haug took a deep dive into the policies\, laws and histo
 ries that contribute to Sebastopol's water pricing. What she found was a K
 alfkaesque maze of procedural sand traps and legal dead ends\, making her 
 question the relationship between bureaucracy and democracy. Looking at t
 he bureaucratic forms which shape the municipal function of water and sewe
 rs\, Haug ponders if the current administrative form delivers the best fun
 ction for Ratepayers.Tonight's talk is a chance to meet your neighbors\, u
 nderstand the systems which control our most vital resource\, our water. U
 nlike City Council meetings\, which are limited by practical necessity\, H
 aug's talk will give a broad history and context. Using a mixture of art 
 history\, performance and audience participation\, Haug's talk bridges the
  gaps in today's partisan politics and asks the question "Does our bureauc
 racy support our democracy?" Kate Haug sits on the City of Sebastopol's W
 ater and Sewer Enterprise Oversight Committee. Her talk is not representat
 ive of the City\, the Water and Sewer Enterprise Oversight Committee and n
 ot authorized by the City of Sebastopol.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                  
 Tickets:\n                \n\n\n\n                      Select Tickets\n  
                   \n$10.00\n$20.00\n$35.00\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n
 \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n      
